+<p class="good"><strong>What good looks like:</strong> One peak where the library preparation or sequencing kit puts it.</p>
+<details>
+<summary>How to read plot 1</summary>
+<div class="howto">
+<p><strong>Worth a look:</strong> A second peak of short reads (adapter dimers, degraded input, failed reads), especially if those reads are unmapped.</p>
+<p><strong>Often benign:</strong> Trimmed short reads form a ramp below the full read length; amplicon libraries show one peak per amplicon.</p>
+<p><strong>How it is calculated:</strong> Files whose median read length is 1 kb or more are drawn in the long-read style: a log length axis here, and positions as % of read length in plots 3-5.</p>
+</div>
+</details>
