+<p class="good"><strong>What good looks like:</strong> One peak at high quality.</p>
+<details>
+<summary>How to read plot 2</summary>
+<div class="howto">
+<p><strong>Worth a look:</strong> A second, low-quality peak, especially if it matches the poorly mapped or unmapped reads.</p>
+<p><strong>Often benign:</strong> Instruments that bin qualities give a few spikes instead of a smooth curve.</p>
+<p><strong>How it is calculated:</strong> Base qualities are averaged as error probabilities, so a few bad bases pull a read down and the values read lower than a plain average of Q scores, which is what FastQC reports. Mean Q at the top of the page and plot 3 are averaged in the same way.</p>
+</div>
+</details>
