+<p class="good"><strong>What good looks like:</strong> Roughly parallel, flat lines, and the same picture in every row.</p>
+<details>
+<summary>How to read plot 4</summary>
+<div class="howto">
+<p><strong>Worth a look:</strong> A row that differs from the MAPQ &gt;= 30 row, such as more N or one base piling up at the start of unmapped or poorly mapped reads (the reason they did not map); an N spike at one position, or a change in composition towards the end of the read (in unaligned input often adapter read-through; aligners usually cut adapters off the alignment, so in aligned input they are not shown).</p>
+<p><strong>Often benign:</strong> Uneven first positions in random-primed libraries; amplicon and bisulfite libraries are uneven by design.</p>
+</div>
+</details>
+</section>
+<section class="plot" id="plot-5" aria-labelledby="plot-5-title">
+<h2 id="plot-5-title"><span class="num">5.</span> Where along the read do errors occur?</h2>
