+<p class="good"><strong>What good looks like:</strong> Roughly parallel, flat lines, and the same picture in every row.</p>
+<details>
+<summary>How to read plot 4</summary>
+<div class="howto">
+<p><strong>Worth a look:</strong> A row that differs from the MAPQ &gt;= 30 row, such as more N or one base piling up at the start of unmapped or poorly mapped reads (the reason they did not map); an N spike at one position, or a change in composition towards the end of the read (in unaligned input often adapter read-through; aligners usually cut adapters off the alignment, so in aligned input they are not shown).</p>
+<p><strong>Often benign:</strong> Uneven first positions in random-primed libraries; amplicon and bisulfite libraries are uneven by design.</p>
+</div>
+</details>
+</section>
+<section class="plot" id="plot-5" aria-labelledby="plot-5-title">
+<h2 id="plot-5-title"><span class="num">5.</span> Where along the read do errors occur?</h2>
+<p class="caption">Mismatches per aligned base at each position, coloured by the read base and one row per MAPQ class; then insertions and deletions, one line per MAPQ class. Each panel has its own vertical scale.</p>
+<div class="figs">
+<p class="plot-key"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="samstat-p5-key-t samstat-p5-key-d" width="325.4" height="25.2" viewBox="0 0 325.4 25.2" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:top" font-family="system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" fill="#1a1a1a"><title id="samstat-p5-key-t">Colour key for the mismatch rows</title><desc id="samstat-p5-key-d">Colour key for the read bases of the mismatch rows: A green; C blue; G orange; T red; N grey. Bottom to top in every mismatch row: A, C, G, T, N.</desc><path fill="none" stroke="#009600" stroke-width="2.5" d="M2,12.6H38"/><text x="44" y="17.5">A</text><path fill="none" stroke="#0000FF" stroke-width="2.5" d="M66.7,12.6H102.7"/><text x="108.7" y="17.5">C</text><path fill="none" stroke="#D17105" stroke-width="2.5" d="M131.4,12.6H167.4"/><text x="173.4" y="17.5">G</text><path fill="none" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="2.5" d="M196,12.6H232"/><text x="238" y="17.5">T</text><path fill="none" stroke="#808080" stroke-width="2.5" d="M260.7,12.6H296.7"/><text x="302.7" y="17.5">N</text></svg>
+</p>
+<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="samstat-p5-t samstat-p5-d" width="640" height="493.8" viewBox="0 0 640 493.8" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:top" font-family="system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" fill="#1a1a1a"><title id="samstat-p5-t">Where along the read do errors occur?</title><desc id="samstat-p5-d">Mismatches, insertions and deletions per aligned base at each position along the read, from position 1 to position 2, aligned part of the read, as percent of aligned bases. One panel per error type, sharing the position axis; each panel has its own vertical scale. Mismatch rows, one per MAPQ class: MAPQ &gt;= 30. Each is a stack of filled areas, one per read base, bottom to top A, C, G, T, N; the top edge of the stack is the total mismatch rate of the class; the colour key is above the figure. Insertion and deletion lines: MAPQ &gt;= 30. A panel labelled none detected has an error rate of zero at every position. A mismatch row is not drawn where fewer than 50 of its reads cover the position or fewer than 50 aligned bases of its class have an MD tag or X operations, a line where fewer than 50 of its reads cover the position.</desc><rect width="640" height="493.8" fill="#fff"/><path fill="none" stroke="#0072B2" stroke-width="2.5" d="M7,17.5H43"/><text x="49" y="22.4">MAPQ &gt;= 30 (10,001 reads)</text><path fill="none" stroke="#e4e4e4" stroke-width="1" d="M77,156.2H619M77,108.2H619M77,60.2H619"/><path fill="none" stroke="#595959" stroke-width="1" d="M77,60.2V156.2H619M348,156.2v4M77,156.2h-4M77,108.2h-4M77,60.2h-4"/><text x="77" y="48.3" font-weight="bold">Mismatches, MAPQ &gt;= 30 (% of aligned bases)</text><text x="70" y="161.1" text-anchor="end">0</text><text x="70" y="113.1" text-anchor="end">2</text><text x="70" y="65.1" text-anchor="end">4</text><text x="348" y="113.1" text-anchor="middle" fill="#595959">none detected</text><path fill="none" stroke="#e4e4e4" stroke-width="1" d="M77,301.2H619M77,253.2H619M77,205.2H619"/><path fill="none" stroke="#595959" stroke-width="1" d="M77,205.2V301.2H619M348,301.2v4M77,301.2h-4M77,253.2h-4M77,205.2h-4"/><text x="77" y="193.3" font-weight="bold">Insertions (% of aligned bases)</text><text x="70" y="306.1" text-anchor="end">0</text><text x="70" y="258.1" text-anchor="end">2</text><text x="70" y="210.1" text-anchor="end">4</text><path fill="none" stroke="#0072B2" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M347.2,301.2H348.8"><title>MAPQ &gt;= 30</title></path><text x="348" y="258.1" text-anchor="middle" fill="#595959">none detected</text><path fill="none" stroke="#e4e4e4" stroke-width="1" d="M77,446.2H619M77,398.2H619M77,350.2H619"/><path fill="none" stroke="#595959" stroke-width="1" d="M77,350.2V446.2H619M348,446.2v4M77,446.2h-4M77,398.2h-4M77,350.2h-4"/><text x="77" y="338.3" font-weight="bold">Deletions (% of aligned bases)</text><text x="348" y="463.7" text-anchor="middle">1</text><text x="348" y="485.4" text-anchor="middle">position in read (bp), aligned part</text><text x="70" y="451.1" text-anchor="end">0</text><text x="70" y="403.1" text-anchor="end">2</text><text x="70" y="355.1" text-anchor="end">4</text><path fill="none" stroke="#0072B2" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M347.2,446.2H348.8"><title>MAPQ &gt;= 30</title></path><text x="348" y="403.1" text-anchor="middle" fill="#595959">none detected</text></svg>
+</div>
+<p class="good"><strong>What good looks like:</strong> Low, flat rates, with MAPQ &gt;= 30 the lowest, and no single base dominating the mismatches.</p>
+<details>
+<summary>How to read plot 5</summary>
+<div class="howto">
+<p><strong>Worth a look:</strong> One base dominating the mismatches at a few positions (for example G at the first positions: bases added during library preparation; N: failed base calls; G towards the 3&#39; end on two-colour instruments: no signal), especially if it reaches further into the read in the low-MAPQ rows; rates that rise towards one end (trim there); errors piled up at the ends of poorly mapped reads (adapters, reads joined from two places); high mismatch rates in well-mapped reads (wrong reference or contamination).</p>
+<p><strong>Often benign:</strong> Low-MAPQ reads are often ambiguous (repeats, reads that fit several places), not necessarily wrong. Long reads carry more insertions and deletions than short reads. A few very long reads can dominate a line.</p>
+</div>
+</details>
+</section>
+<section class="plot" id="plot-6" aria-labelledby="plot-6-title">
+<h2 id="plot-6-title"><span class="num">6.</span> How accurate are the aligned reads?</h2>
